From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karol Herbst <kherbst@redhat.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 12:00:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nir/serialize: set info.spec to NULL

We have to clear the pointer to NULL otherwise we'll serialize the pointer
value breaking shader cache key generation.

Fixes: d8b21cc8ea6 ("vtn,nir: print shader filename and spec constants")
Reviewed-by: Rob Clark <robclark@freedesktop.org>
(cherry picked from commit c3b008c1ba01d455351b762253ef44c3ca19653f)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44489>
(cherry picked from commit c4b4fbfa68a164330825fd385124d7e29e8dd67d)
---
 src/compiler/nir/nir_serialize.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/compiler/nir/nir_serialize.c b/src/compiler/nir/nir_serialize.c
index 2095a2ae5e2..4934427ebe2 100644
--- a/src/compiler/nir/nir_serialize.c
+++ b/src/compiler/nir/nir_serialize.c
@@ -2229,7 +2229,7 @@ serialize_internal(struct blob *blob, const nir_shader *nir, bool strip, bool se
       blob_write_string(blob, info.label);
    if (!strip && info.spec)
       blob_write_string(blob, info.spec);
-   info.name = info.label = NULL;
+   info.name = info.label = info.spec = NULL;
    blob_write_bytes(blob, (uint8_t *)&info, sizeof(info));
 
    write_var_list(&ctx, &nir->variables);
-- 
